AUTONOMOUS BEACH ROBOT — TESTING GUIDE
========================================

MODES AT A GLANCE
-----------------
  A) Full sim          — no hardware at all; one command starts everything
  B) Indoor / desk     — real camera, no ESP32/IMU; safety checks disabled
  C) Hardware in loop  — real everything; standard production launch
  D) Standalone tools  — model, detector, tracker tested outside ROS


═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
MODE A — FULL SIMULATION (no hardware required)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Starts: fake_hardware.py + fake_camera.py + all ROS nodes
Safety disabled automatically: IMU safety, camera safety
FSM watchdog: STUCK watchdog still runs (fake odometry satisfies it)

Terminal 1 — launch everything:
  ros2 launch robot_bringup sim.launch.py

  With a specific test image:
  ros2 launch robot_bringup sim.launch.py \
    image_path:=/home/ttkan/AutonomousBeachRobot/tools/test_trash2.jpg

  With a different model:
  ros2 launch robot_bringup sim.launch.py \
    model_path:=/home/ttkan/AutonomousBeachRobot/ml/models/trash_v3_best.onnx

Terminal 2 — arm and drive state machine:

  Start mission (CALIBRATE → SCAN):
    ros2 topic pub --once /mission_control/command std_msgs/msg/String "data: START"

  Inject detection → SCAN will enter TRACK (area 4500 = small, not pickup size):
    ros2 topic pub --once /trash_detections std_msgs/msg/String \
      "data: '{\"cx\": 320.0, \"cy\": 240.0, \"area\": 4500, \"conf\": 0.85, \"tracking\": false, \"bbox\": [290, 210, 350, 270]}'"

  Trigger PICKUP (norm_area = 50000/307200 ≈ 0.163, above 0.15 threshold):
    ros2 topic pub --once /trash_detections std_msgs/msg/String \
      "data: '{\"cx\": 320.0, \"cy\": 240.0, \"area\": 50000, \"conf\": 0.85, \"tracking\": true, \"bbox\": [100, 100, 540, 380]}'"

  Simulate approaching trash (gradual area increase):
    python3 /home/ttkan/AutonomousBeachRobot/tools/tracking_loop_tester.py

  Stop mission:
    ros2 topic pub --once /mission_control/command std_msgs/msg/String "data: STOP"

Optional — view the camera feed from your PC (no ROS2 needed on PC):
  python3 /home/troykaneshiro/AutonomousBeachRobot/tools/stream_camera.py
  # Then open http://<pi-ip>:8080 in any browser on the same network.
  # Live YOLO bounding boxes are overlaid when detections are active.
  # Custom port: python3 tools/stream_camera.py --port 9090

NOTE: sim_mode=true is set automatically by sim.launch.py — the TRACK loss
timeout is disabled, so a single --once publication holds TRACK indefinitely.


═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
MODE B — INDOOR / DESK TESTING (real camera, no ESP32)
═══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

Use when you have a USB camera but no robot hardware.
Safety channels are disabled so IMU noise and non-sand images don't fire STOP events.
STUCK watchdog stays active — supply fake odometry if you don't have wheel encoders.

Terminal 1 — launch nodes (disable both safety channels):
  ros2 launch robot_bringup beach_robot.launch.py \
    disable_imu_safety:=true disable_camera_safety:=true

  Disable only camera safety (e.g. outdoors but testing on concrete/grass):
  ros2 launch robot_bringup beach_robot.launch.py disable_camera_safety:=true

  Disable only IMU safety (surface is sand but IMU not calibrated):
  ros2 launch robot_bringup beach_robot.launch.py disable_imu_safety:=true

Terminal 2 — supply fake hardware data so the FSM doesn't stall:

  Fake odometry (prevents STUCK watchdog firing — run continuously):
    ros2 topic pub -r 50 /wheel/odometry nav_msgs/msg/Odometry \
      "{pose: {pose: {position: {x: $(python3 -c 'import time; print(time.time()%100)'), y: 0.0}}}}"

  Simpler: just run fake_hardware.py alongside:
    python3 /home/ttkan/AutonomousBeachRobot/tools/fake_hardware.py

  Fake IMU (if terrain_monitor is enabled and you need calibration data):
    ros2 topic pub -r 100 /imu/data sensor_msgs/msg/Imu \
      "{linear_acceleration: {x: 0.0, y: 0.0, z: 9.81}}"

Terminal 3 — optional camera viewer (see Mode A for details):
  python3 /home/troykaneshiro/AutonomousBeachRobot/tools/stream_camera.py

Terminal 4 — arm and test:
  (same pub commands as Mode A)


